# Sensitive paths for shipping-work's Step 1.5 doc spot-check (#281).
# One path per line; `#`-comments and blank lines ignored. This file REPLACES
# doc-check.sh's built-in defaults rather than extending them.
#
# Entries match whole path SEGMENTS at any depth (gregoryfoster/skills#252).
# Two entries therefore reach further than their name suggests, and both
# over-matches are kept deliberately — do not narrow them:
#   deploy/   also reaches tests/deploy/, whose two tests assert the installed
#             unit and the unit-only notifier credential; both are documented
#             in DEPLOYMENT.md / ENVIRONMENT.md, so a hit there is a fair ask
#   scripts/  also reaches tests/scripts/ and the six vendored skill symlinks
#             under skills/*/scripts/. The entry earns its place on COMMANDS.md
#             alone; the extra hits are the price of not anchoring it
# For a spot-check that exits 1 and asks a human to look, over-matching is the
# cheap failure; the miss that exits 0 is the expensive one. Narrowing either
# one means listing files individually, which is the under-match #252 fixed.
#
# Dropped from the defaults because nothing in this repo matches them —
# a dead entry reads as coverage of a tree we do not have:
#   schema.sql     — no raw-SQL schema; Alembic owns the schema
#   src/models/    — models live under src/core/models/, covered by src/core/
#   .env.example   — env files are never committed (tests/test_env_files_are_not_committable.py)
#
# Guarded by tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py.

